From 2eab4fd795b7665fdeabc2ebf7f503d9557fe34c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oscar Nordstrom <13300531+n0rpan@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 19:00:19 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] ggml-cpu: persistent file-backed cache for repacked
 weights (GGML_CPU_REPACK_CACHE)

Opt-in via GGML_CPU_REPACK_CACHE=<dir>; unset keeps the old behaviour.
The CPU_REPACK buffer becomes a page-aligned anonymous mmap; on a cache hit the
tensor pages are replaced with a MAP_PRIVATE|MAP_FIXED mapping of the cached
payload, so warm loads skip the repack and the weights are file-backed.
Misses repack in memory, write atomically (tmp + fsync + rename) and map the
written inode. The full key (build, patch id, cpu features, repack layout probe,
tensor shape, model file identity or source hash) is stored in each header;
any mismatch, corruption or I/O error falls back to the in-memory repack and
prints a parseable "ggml-repack-cache: ERROR <reason> ..." line.

Adds tests/test-repack-cache.cpp, tools/repack_cache.py (list/prune/clear)
and docs/repack-cache.md.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
