From: Oscar Nordstrom <13300531+n0rpan@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 19:33:21 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] ggml-cpu: repack cache: verify once on write, sampled
 pages on hits

GGML_CPU_REPACK_CACHE_VERIFY now defaults to "once": the payload is hashed
while writing and re-hashed from the written file before the header is marked
verified=1 and renamed into place. Warm hits keep the cheap checks and compare
8 evenly spaced 4 KiB windows against hashes stored in the header (format 2).
"1"/"full" keeps the full hash on every hit, "0"/"off" skips the samples.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
