From cb20e63c3aee76afc4241c5661ebda26b4b7860b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oscar Nordstrom <13300531+n0rpan@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 19:38:22 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] ggml-cpu: GGML_CPU_REPACK_DROP_SOURCE: release source
 pages of repacked tensors

Opt-in (GGML_CPU_REPACK_DROP_SOURCE=1), independent of the repack cache: after
a tensor is repacked or served from the cache, the page-aligned interior of its
source range is released with madvise(MADV_DONTNEED) (shared/read-only mappings
only) and posix_fadvise(POSIX_FADV_DONTNEED) on the backing file, so the GGUF
copy of repacked weights stops being charged to the cgroup. Partial pages at the
range ends are kept.

Also fix the source-file lookup on btrfs/overlayfs: /proc/self/maps reports a
different device than st_dev there, so the identity check now compares the
inode only. Before this, every tensor on btrfs fell back to src=content.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
